  {
    "sha": "b0a046a9e13bdce9ddbf836e138d54ebe65355ad",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKGIwYTA0NmE5ZTEzYmRjZTlkZGJmODM2ZTEzOGQ1NGViZTY1MzU1YWQ",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-09T03:03:03Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-09T03:03:03Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(ui): preview the incoming stock in the viewport on the setup page\n\nWhile a setup's settings page is open and its stock source is \"What\n<previous setup> leaves behind\", the viewport draws the body the setups\nbefore it leave (stock_sim::incoming_body's display sheet) as a teal\ntranslucent stock-slot part, apart from the setup's own Stock node.\n\n- app: setup_stock_view::incoming_shape measures the incoming body once\n  (box, volume and the sheet as triangles), carried into the active\n  setup's frame (A_active * A_setup^-1; identity when the setup is the\n  active one).\n- ui: incoming_view caches it in State keyed by (setup, active setup,\n  doc_version), refreshed at the end of drain_actions; it measures only\n  when the key moves and drops the mesh the moment the page closes,\n  another page opens or the setup takes its own stock. The page's box\n  and volume read the same measurement (one program sim per version).\n- viewport: fs_stock paints class 4 as the incoming-stock teal.\n\nA refusal draws nothing, is logged once per measurement and stays on\nthe page as before. View state only - no command, nothing undoable.\n\nFixes #406\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
