      },
      "message": "fix(app): the incoming stock is drawn as a closed block, not a buried top sheet\n\nHand check of #519, root cause: incoming_shape returned only the body's\ndisplay sheet - its TOP (115 200 facets at Z 12 on the test project) -\nand the part spanning Z 0..16 over the same footprint hid it in every\nview. setup_stock_shell::floor_and_walls closes it: a floor quad under\nevery material column and a wall wherever a column's [floor, top] is\nnot covered by its neighbour's (the outline and every cut step), mapped\ninto the view frame like the sheet.\n\nPinned by setup_stock_view::the_incoming_stock_is_a_closed_block (every\nedge shared by exactly two facets) and the_sheet_stands_in_the_active_\nsetups_frame (the mesh now spans the body's floor..top; carried back to\nSetup1's frame it spans Z -2 .. 16).\n\nRefs #406\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
